    <!-- BIOS / WoL Checklist Guide -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_CardBiosGuideTitle">⚙️ BIOS/UEFI Checklist for Wake-on-LAN</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_CardBiosGuideBadge">Required 1x Setup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_CardBiosGuideDesc">To allow lab PCs to be powered on remotely when fully shut down, verify the following motherboard BIOS/UEFI settings:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_BiosItem1Title">1. Disable ErP / EuP Ready (CRITICAL)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_BiosItem1Desc">ErP cuts standby power to the LAN port when shut down. Change ErP/EuP to 'Disabled' so the ethernet LED stays active.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_BiosItem2Title">2. Enable 'Wake on LAN' / 'PCIe PME Event'</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_BiosItem2Desc">Under the Power Management / ACPI BIOS menu, enable 'Power On by PCI-E/PME Device' or 'Resume by Onboard LAN'.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_BiosItem3Title">3. Verify Ethernet Port LED Status</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_BiosItem3Desc">When the PC is shut down, verify that the rear RJ-45 LAN port LED remains lit/blinking, indicating the PHY chip is ready for Magic Packets.</sys:String>

